  "ingredients": [
    "1/2 cup macadamia nuts",
    "1/4 cup erythritol",
    "1/2 cup almond flour",
    "1/4 cup butter (chilled)",
    "1 large egg yolk",
    "8 ounce cream cheese (softened)",
    "1/4 cup butter (softened)",
    "2 large egg",
    "1/4 cup erythritol",
    "1/4 teaspoon liquid stevia",
    "2 tablespoon key lime zest",
    "2 tablespoon key lime juice (~2 limes)"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat oven to 350F. Add the macadamia nuts to a food processor.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-key-lime-cheesecakes/#wprm-recipe-51053-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/IMG_1128.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Grind the nuts into a coarse meal and add the erythritol.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-key-lime-cheesecakes/#wprm-recipe-51053-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/IMG_1136.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pulse for a few moments and then add the almond flour. Pulse again until well combined.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-key-lime-cheesecakes/#wprm-recipe-51053-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/IMG_1139.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cube the chilled butter and add it to the food processor. Pulse again until the mixture is beginning to clump.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-key-lime-cheesecakes/#wprm-recipe-51053-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/IMG_1142.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the egg yolk and pulse again until the dough is beginning to clump.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-key-lime-cheesecakes/#wprm-recipe-51053-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/IMG_1143.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove the dough from the food processor and knead together.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-key-lime-cheesecakes/#wprm-recipe-51053-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/IMG_1148.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using silicone cupcake molds (or just a regular greased cupcake tin), fill the wells about 1/8 to 1/4 of the way full.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-key-lime-cheesecakes/#wprm-recipe-51053-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/IMG_1151.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake for 5–7 minutes. The crusts will still look greasy and undercooked when taken out. Leave oven on.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-key-lime-cheesecakes/#wprm-recipe-51053-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/IMG_1154.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "While the crust is baking, prepare the filling. Beat together the cream cheese and butter.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-key-lime-cheesecakes/#wprm-recipe-51053-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/IMG_1157.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the eggs and mix to combine.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-key-lime-cheesecakes/#wprm-recipe-51053-step-0-9",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/IMG_1159.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the erythritol and liquid stevia and mix to combine.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-key-lime-cheesecakes/#wprm-recipe-51053-step-0-10",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/IMG_1161.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Finally, add in the lime zest and lime juice. Mix again until fully combined.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-key-lime-cheesecakes/#wprm-recipe-51053-step-0-11",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/IMG_1162.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once the crusts are out of the oven, let cool for about 3–5 minutes, and then pour the cheesecake mixture into the molds. Leave a little space at the top to prevent them from spilling over as they rise.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-key-lime-cheesecakes/#wprm-recipe-51053-step-0-12",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/IMG_1164.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake for 30–35 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-key-lime-cheesecakes/#wprm-recipe-51053-step-0-13",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/IMG_1167.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cool the cheesecakes for 20–30 minutes and store in the fridge overnight.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-key-lime-cheesecakes/#wprm-recipe-51053-step-0-14",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/IMG_1170.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve and enjoy!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-key-lime-cheesecakes/#wprm-recipe-51053-step-0-15",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
